00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.909 align:start position:0%
 
we all strive to be healthier versions  of ourselves and improve our overall  well-being  most of the time we tend to concentrate  only on the body focusing on our  physical health such as exercising daily  and eating a well-balanced diet while  this is extremely important it is not  the only component of total well-being  that we should be improving  your mind is equally just as important  and we need to nurture our mental health  the mind-body connection is the link  between a person's thoughts attitudes  and behaviors and their physical health  the mind and the body are not two  separate entities although they are  often treated that way your physical  health and emotional health are  intertwined in what's known as the  mind-body connection  how you think can affect how you feel  and how you feel can affect how you  think hence that's why we often hear the  saying your thoughts become your reality  have you ever felt your stomach tighten  up when you were anxious or have you  experienced high levels of stress at  work which caused you to have trouble  sleeping well  that's you experiencing the mind and  body connection  it is important to note that the mind  does not mean the brain  the mind consists of mental states such  as the thoughts beliefs attitudes and  emotions whereas think of our brain as  the hardware that allows us to  experience these mental states our  mental states can be fully conscious or  subconscious we can have emotional  reactions to situations without being  aware of why we are reacting a certain  way and each mental state has a  physiology associated with it whether  it's positive or negative response felt  in the physical body for instance  constant worry and stress over our jobs  finances or family issues can cause your  body to react as if it is under attack  your body releases hormones that speed  up your heart rate and breathing  increases blood pressure and make your  muscles tense this physical reaction is  called the fight of flight stress  response if you're constantly feeling  this way this can lead to high blood  pressure as well as other mental issues  which can cause depression or anxiety  on the other hand what we do with our  physical body such as what we eat and  how much we exercise can also impact our  mental state if you live an inactive  life and eat crappy food you will  constantly lack an energy struggle to  focus and feel moody however if you eat  a well-balanced diet and exercise on a  regular basis your body will produce  endorphins making you feel good and  boost your energy levels as well as your  positive attitude a healthy body keeps  you well and active and a healthy mind  keeps you focused and engaged hence to  achieve total wellness it's not one or  the other but it's about bringing  balance and harmony to the mind and body  do you sometimes feel lifeless or bored  do you dread each coming day and feel  like you're merely existing instead of  really living you feel like you're not  making progress and time flies really  quickly well  stop living life on autopilot making  unconscious automatic decisions that  don't align with how you want to work  and live the single most important step  is to become more aware of our mental  states to increase the consciousness in  our thoughts attitudes beliefs and  physical actions or reactions  once you're aware of what you want  you can align your thoughts and actions  so here are four simple steps to  increase the mind and body connection  have you seen the movie inside out the  film is so brilliant in depicting our  emotions visually sometimes it's so hard  for us to express or visualize how we  think and feel so a fun way is to look  at our emotions as those characters  portrayed in the movie when we imagine a  situation the primal parts of the brain  react as if it was really happening  therefore positive visualization can  help you control or manage your emotions  so ask yourself these questions what am  i thinking and feeling think of the  characters in the movie how is that  affecting my physical body am i tensed  up is my heart rate increasing rapidly  how can i change that and negative  thoughts or emotions to a more positive  one and bring about balance to my mind  and body  by asking yourself these questions  you're bringing awareness to your  thoughts and attitude hence you're able  to take control of your mind and change  the outcome to a more positive one  sometimes we talk to ourselves self-talk  is your internet dialogue it is  influenced by your subconscious mind and  it reveals your thoughts beliefs and  ideas self-talk can be both negative and  positive  positive self-talk is an inner monologue  that makes you feel really good about  yourself and boosts your self-esteem it  is an optimistic voice in your head that  encourages you to look at the bright  side pick yourself up when you fall and  this can enhance your performance  the world's greatest athletes might not  always be the strongest physically or  the most skillful however they are  mentally strong and they often have a  positive inner monologue with themselves  what they tell themselves right before  the competition can determine the  outcome  if you believe your self-talk is often  too negative  let's learn to shift that inner  monologue here are some examples  i'm overweight and so out of shape i  might as well not bother and stop trying  well i'm capable and strong and i want  to get healthier for me i've never done  this before and i'm pretty sure i'm  gonna fail at it this is a wonderful  opportunity for me to learn from others  and grow farming new habits take time  and effort but if you start to become  aware of your inner monologue positive  self-talk can become your norm so here  are some tips i've been practicing to  build up a more positive self-talk  give yourself positive affirmations  seeing positive words or inspiring  images can be enough to redirect your  thoughts this can be as simple as having  positive affirmations in your home or  office or on your phone well basically  anywhere you spend a significant amount  of time  don't take yourself so seriously so what  if you mess up when we take ourselves  too seriously we believe that everything  revolves around us that's why we fear  being ridiculed and this stops us from  trying when you learn to loosen up on  yourself you open up space for play and  exploration and for change  surround yourself with positive people  whether you notice it or not we absorb  the energy and emotions of people around  us this includes both negative and  positive so choose to surround yourself  with positive people who encourages you  we all know that we should be looking  after our bodies eat well and move more  that's because how well your body feels  can also have an impact on your mind i  exercise regularly and eat a  well-balanced diet because i love how it  makes me feel i'm energetic throughout  the day i'm able to sleep better i feel  more relaxed and have a more positive  outlook in my life for me i love to lift  weights and perform heat exercises when  i workout i'm in my own zone where i'm  really in tune with my own body and with  what i want to accomplish and this helps  me to build a stronger mindset as well  so don't just exercise mindlessly be in  the moment be in tune with your own body  and this can help you to push further  especially when you feel like giving up  there are many other forms of exercise  that you can also incorporate which  focuses on the mind and body connection  such as yoga tai chi qi gong and pilates  when it comes to food we often hear this  saying you are what you eat  there's actually a lot of truth in that  food is fuel food fills your brain and  body and the fuel you choose will  directly affect the structure and  function of your body and brain this  doesn't have to be complicated stick  with the basics fill your body with high  quality real foods that nourishes the  brain reduce on processed foods and  refined sugars because over time  consuming too much junk can cause  inflammation in the body mood disorders  as well as other mental and body  illnesses  relationships are one of the most  important aspects of our lives yet we  often forget just how crucial our  connections with other people are for  our physical and mental well-being  people who are more socially connected  to their family friends and community  are happier physically healthier and  live longer with fewer mental health  problems compared to those who are  isolated or less connected having close  positive relationships can give us a  sense of purpose and belonging it's not  just how many friends you have but it's  the quality of your relationships that  matters how we interact and form  relationships has changed so much over  the past decade nowadays we're so hooked  up on social media and the online world  that we have often forgotten what it  feels like to have a meaningful  relationship with someone you might have  lots of friends online but if you are in  need for emotional support  do you really have someone that you can  call and turn to  here are three things you can do to  start building positive relationships  invest your time yep  you need to consciously put time aside  to connect with your family and friends  that means don't work long hours or even  the weekends  be present yes you're physically with  your family and friends however do you  catch yourself engaging on your phone  instead of engaging with them  you don't always have to be online  because those online friends aren't real  relationships be present connect and  spend time talking and doing things with  your family and friends  recognize unhealthy relationships  living in conflict or within a toxic  relationship is more damaging than being  alone and this can negatively affect our  mental and physical health so  recognizing this can help us to get out  of it move forward and find solutions to  issues while we still have a lot to  learn about the mind and body connection  there is no doubt that taking care of  our mental health is just as important  as our physical health the mind-body  connection isn't just about how the mind  affects the body it is also about how  the body affects the mind hence making  healthy lifestyle choices is an  important part of maintaining the  balance between mind and body i hope  that this video has taught you to be  more aware of your mind your thoughts  because it will also affect your  physical health if you enjoyed this  video do give this video a thumbs up let  me know in the comments below and do  also hit the subscribe button if you  haven't yet done it okay so remember to  continue to stay active eat a  well-balanced diet and let's look after  our mental health as well all the best

